{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>I am HaShem who brought you out of the land of Egypt.</b> And from the foundation of Rabbi Moshe ha-Darshan: the four strands in it correspond to the eight days that Israel spent from the time they left Egypt until they said song at the sea — each strand is folded in half, making eight threads. And if you ask: in the portion of Beshalch, did Rashi not say — on the seventh night they went down into the sea, and at morning they said song? Rather, one may say that here, where he counts eight days, he counts from the day they departed from Goshen and assembled at Raamses; whereas there, in the portion of Beshalch, he counts from the day they traveled from Raamses to Sukkot. The order of the portion of Shalah is complete."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The Hebrew phrase 'ושמונה חוטים שבה כנגד שמונה ימים' omits any explicit mention of the four tzitzit strands that are doubled to make eight threads; the translator has supplied this connection from context. The final line 'שלימא סדרא' is a colophon marking the end of the portion."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:11.240204356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}